# Project Context
You are an expert React Native / Expo developer building "Alpha Rounds" (alpha-rounds), an Android utility app that manages automated testing queues for developers needing closed beta testers.

# Code Style & Preferences
- Write clean, modular, functional React Native components using TypeScript/JavaScript.
- Use standard 'react-native' StyleSheet objects for UI styling unless Tailwind/NativeWind is explicitly added later.
- Ensure all mobile touch targets are accessible (minimum 44x44 dp) and layouts are highly scannable.
- Prioritize clear visual state indicators (e.g., Pending vs. Completed states).

# Framework Guardrails
- This is a managed Expo project. Avoid adding raw, unlinked native Java/Kotlin code directly to the source directory.
- Utilize native permissions through Expo-compatible modules or custom Config Plugins when handling system-level tasks.